{"type":"message","id":"3df5ef7c","parentId":"6deebab6","timestamp":"2026-04-08T19:05:06.552Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the cron jobs. The hourly group learning job (`49f9b6b8-cb9d-4765-89bf-039c22e5b1ca`) is running every hour (`0 * * * *`) and has had 5 consecutive errors. The issue is clear: it runs every hour, including at night (22:00-03:00) when the API is unavailable.\n\nLet me update the cron job to only run during working hours (07:00-21:00). The cron expression would be: `0 7,9,11,13,15,17,19,21 * * *` - this runs at 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19, and 21 minutes past the hour.\n \nActually, I need to think through the timing more carefully. The cron runs at minute 0 of every hour, but I need it to execute during business hours when the API is actually available. Looking at the data, the API worked fine at 06:02 and 07:02, so I should adjust the cron expression to target those hours when there's actual activity.\n\nLet me use a simpler approach and just specify the hours directly: `0 7,9,11,13,15,17,19,21 * * *` means it runs at 07:00, 09:00, 11:00, and so on through 21:00. That covers the working hours I need without the complexity of ranges.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I can see the hourly cron has run every hour including nighttime (22:00-07:00) when the API is unavailable. Let me optimize it to only run during working hours:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dvk7qvku0j2m_1","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"update","jobId":"49f9b6b8-cb9d-4765-89bf-039c22e5b1ca","patch":{"schedule":{"expr":"0 7,9,11,13,15,17,19,21 * * *","kind":"cron","tz":"Asia/Shanghai","staggerMs":300000},"description":"每小时学习飞书群消息，积累酒店知识（仅工作时段07:00-21:00，因飞书OAuth夜间22:00-07:00失效）"}}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":5943,"output":522,"cacheRead":59131,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65596,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRea